WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.800
- Do you have advice for young minds today

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.210
dreaming about, creating
as you have dreamt,

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.290
creating intelligence systems?

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:12.800
What is the best way to arrive
at new breakthrough ideas

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.350
and carry them through
the fire of criticism

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.433
and past conventional ideas?

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.240
- Ask your questions.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:28.053
Really, your questions are never dumb.

00:00:29.045 --> 00:00:29.878
(laughs)

00:00:29.878 --> 00:00:30.978
And so is your own way

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.432
and don't take no for an answer.

00:00:34.432 --> 00:00:36.510
(chuckles)

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.790
If they're really dumb,
you will find out quickly,

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.280
by trial and error,

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.380
to see that they're not leading any place.

00:00:45.227 --> 00:00:50.227
But, follow them and try to
understand things your way.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.000
That is my advice.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.390
I don't know if it's gonna help anyone.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:57.833
- [Interviewer] No,
that's brilliantly put.

00:00:57.833 --> 00:00:58.730
- There is a lot of

00:01:01.446 --> 00:01:02.630
inertia

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.603
in science, in academia.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.873
It is slowing down science.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.730
- [Interviewer] Yeah
those two words: your way,

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.444
that's a powerful thing.

00:01:14.444 --> 00:01:17.510
It's against inertia, potentially.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.410
Against the full,

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.290
- [Older Man] Against your professor.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:21.880
- Against your professor.
(laughs)

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.720
- I wrote a book of why,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.553
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:01:24.553 --> 00:01:27.260
In order to democratize common sense.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:28.234
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:30.110
(both laugh)

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.050
In order to instill,

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:36.820
rebellious spirits in students.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:41.755
So, they wouldn't wait until
the professor get things right.

00:01:41.755 --> 00:01:44.172
(both laugh)

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:46.387
- [Interviewer] So,
you wrote the manifesto

00:01:46.387 --> 00:01:49.520
"The Rebellion Against the Professor".

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.473
- [Older Man] Against the professor, yes.

